The questions I would ask in the room are:
1. What would we expect to see if first useful activity varies by branch?
2. What evidence would instead support that some customer types need assisted=
 follow-up?
3. How do we rule out that card or online activation friction delays use?

This has returned because the previous answer was useful but not strong enoug=
h to become a standing rule. Use January 2024 as the new evidence point rathe=
r than recycling the earlier conclusion. Please work towards where branch coa=
ching or onboarding process changes are needed. A useful output would be a on=
e-page finding note plus the underlying CSV for our own review.

Use monthly customer and KYC snapshots; monthly account snapshots, status eve=
nts, limits, product enrolments and signatories; available initial-deposit re=
cords up to the request date; transaction-level timestamps, channels, amounts=
